		wayland.ArgValue(flags),
	])!
	return wl.WlBuffer{
		Object: buffer_id_object
	}
}

// Set the device the compositor should import the dmabufs to for sampling in
// the next create or create_immed request. To avoid race conditions when the
// compositor removes a device from the tranches, it is not a protocol error
// if the device hasn't been advertised by the compositor in a tranche with
// the sampling flag, but the import is likely to fail in that case. If the
// client doesn't know a suitable target device, it shouldn't set one, and
// the compositor should attempt import on all devices it supports. If the
// array is too small to contain a dev_t or larger than required, the
// invalid_dev_t_size error will be emitted.
pub fn (proxy &ZwpLinuxBufferParamsV1) set_sampling_device(device []u8) ! {
	proxy.conn.request(proxy.id, 4, [wayland.ArgValue(device)])!
}

